228 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 166 0 R
/T (A signed JWT stays valid until it expires [6][7], so withdrawal alone cannot stop a token already issued. Checking with the server on every request adds an extra network call [8][9]. ConsentGuard uses short-lived tokens verified locally, plus a fast consent-counter \(cv\) check against a local cache.)
/E (A signed JWT stays valid until it expires [6][7], so withdrawal alone cannot stop a token already issued. Checking with the server on every request adds an extra network call [8][9]. ConsentGuard uses short-lived tokens verified locally, plus a fast consent-counter \(cv\) check against a local cache.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
229 0 obj
<<
