/T (Evidence must be tamper-evident)
/E (Evidence must be tamper-evident)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
230 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 166 0 R
/T (Under GDPR, Controllers must be able to demonstrate consent [3], and the DPDP Rules require logs to be retained for at least one year [2]. Each audit event stores the hash of the previous one, so editing or deleting a record breaks the chain and the verifier detects it [10][11]. This detects tampering. It does not prevent it.)
/E (Under GDPR, Controllers must be able to demonstrate consent [3], and the DPDP Rules require logs to be retained for at least one year [2]. Each audit event stores the hash of the previous one, so editing or deleting a record breaks the chain and the verifier detects it [10][11]. This detects tampering. It does not prevent it.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
