<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 166 0 R
/T (Consent must be tied to a specific purpose. The DPDP Act 2023 requires consent to be free, specific, informed and unambiguous \(s.6\) [1], and GDPR requires purpose limitation and withdrawal as easy as giving consent \(Art. 5\(1\)\(b\), 7\(3\)\) [3]. ConsentGuard records a separate consent for each of three purposes.)
/E (Consent must be tied to a specific purpose. The DPDP Act 2023 requires consent to be free, specific, informed and unambiguous \(s.6\) [1], and GDPR requires purpose limitation and withdrawal as easy as giving consent \(Art. 5\(1\)\(b\), 7\(3\)\) [3]. ConsentGuard records a separate consent for each of three purposes.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [17]
>>
endobj
237 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 166 0 R
/T (Consent is only meaningful for the notice the user actually saw [1][5]. Each notice has a version number \(nv\). Consent is stored with the nv it was given against. If a material change is published, consent for the affected purpose is treated as outdated and the user is asked again)
/E (Consent is only meaningful for the notice the user actually saw [1][5]. Each notice has a version number \(nv\). Consent is stored with the nv it was given against. If a material change is published, consent for the affected purpose is treated as outdated and the user is asked again)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [18]
>>
