/Title (Under GDPR, Controllers must be able to demonstrate consent [3], and the DPDP Rules require logs to be retained for at least one year [2]. Each audit event stores the hash of the previous one, so editing or deleting a record breaks the chain and the verifier detects it [10][11]. This detects tampering. It does not prevent it.)
